\anchor hdEmbree_mainpage

## Runtime overview

This generated page is for Hydra integrators. It is authoritative only for the
plugin's external runtime contract and intentionally omits internal API/module
detail.

Typhoon is the CPU path-tracing Hydra render delegate implemented by the
`hdEmbree` plugin. Hydra discovers renderer identity `Embree` and creates
`HdEmbreeRendererPlugin` through `plugInfo.json`.

During Hydra synchronization, delegate adapters pull dirty mesh, instance,
material, light, camera, and render-buffer data into renderer-owned records.
Scene mutation stops background rendering and advances a scene version. A
render pass then translates camera, framing, Hydra lighting presentation, AOV,
active RenderSettings, and delegate-setting state into `ty::Renderer`, which
commits the Embree scene, traces progressive samples, and writes Hydra render
buffers.

The delegate owns the Embree device, root scene, renderer, and render thread.
Meshes own prototype and instance contexts whose stable addresses Embree
borrows as geometry user data. `CommitResources()` does no BVH work; scene
commit is deferred until renderer setup has validated the scene and AOVs.
Failed setup parks usable buffers but cannot publish a valid frame or write a
stale RenderProduct.

## Supported external contract

hdEmbree installs no hand-written C++ headers and exposes no supported
hand-written C++ API. Its extension mechanisms are plugin registration and the
USD render-settings schema, not its internal C++ module boundaries.

- `plugInfo.json` registers renderer identity `Embree`,
  `HdEmbreeRendererPlugin`, the implicit-surface scene-index plugin, and
  `TyphoonRenderSettingsAPI`.
- `TyphoonRenderSettingsAPI` is an applied API schema auto-applied to
  `RenderSettings`. Renderer-specific attributes use the `ty:` namespace;
  names, types, defaults, and allowed tokens are defined by
  `schema/schema.usda`.
- Hydra applications may also use direct delegate settings. The standard
  `renderingColorSpace` attribute and generic `domeLightCameraVisibility` and
  `enableExposureCompensation` settings are deliberately unnamespaced.
- Lit or unlit color presentation follows
  `HdRenderPassState::GetLightingEnabled()` rather than a Typhoon render
  setting. Lit mode path traces the lights supplied after Hydra scene-light
  pruning; unlit mode displays authored `displayColor` without material or
  light evaluation. A lightless lit scene receives no headlight or ambient
  fallback.
- Material render-context priority supports `mtlx` and `default`.
- The delegate supports standard color, depth, normal, and ID AOVs, the
  `adaptiveHeatmap` and `ambocc` diagnostics, and float-vector primvar outputs.
  `README.md` defines the authoritative names and formats.
- Progressive radiance rendering always uses adaptive sampling. The
  `adaptiveHeatmap` diagnostic is computed only when its AOV is bound and does
  not replace color output.
- Ambient visibility is computed only when `ambocc` is bound, at one AO ray
  per progressive pixel sample, and never attenuates color output.
- Legacy viewport clients that bind no AOVs receive anonymous color and depth
  buffers whose completion drives render-pass convergence. Valid camera
  framing without AOV bindings remains unsupported and settles as a failed
  frame.
- The Linux Houdini 22 package registers `HdEmbreeRendererPlugin` as
  `Typhoon` in Houdini. It is rebuilt against the host installation's OpenUSD
  0.26.5, Embree 3, OpenImageIO, Imath, TBB, C++20, and standard-library ABI;
  it does not load the normal Pixi versions of those libraries.

Offline clients set `enableInteractive = false`. After a valid frame converges,
the render pass writes active stage-authored RenderProducts through Hio.
Interactive clients leave the setting unset or true and consume render buffers
without writing product files.

See the user-facing settings, AOV formats, examples, and limitations in
`README.md`. See ownership, frame/path flow, invariants, and extension points in
`ARCHITECTURE.md`. Contributor commands and mandatory editing rules are in
`AGENTS.md`.
*/
